// WHAT THIS IS FOR: a map whose Reasons view is first laid out while its pane is HIDDEN -- as it
// is when a file opens straight into the Mechanism arrangement -- and then shown.
//
// In a hidden pane every text measures 0 wide. The wrapping measurement already knew to throw such
// a zero away; the single-line one, which cuts a premise row to its box and stops the inference
// bar where the rule's name begins, cached it. Back in Reasons, every row "fitted", so none was
// cut and the long ones ran out past the box, and the bar ran on through the rule's name. Found
// on Moore 1939, 17 Oct 2026.
//
// WHAT TO SEE, after a hidden first layout:
//   - premise (1), far longer than the box is wide, cut with an ellipsis INSIDE the box
//   - the bars stopping short of "EG" and "MP", never running through them
//
// IF THE DEFECT IS PRESENT: premise (1) runs on past the right-hand edge of the box, and a line
// is struck through each rule name. Kept by app/test_rendered_dom.mjs (hiddenFirstLayoutChecks).

[External things exist]: At least two things outside our minds exist now.

<Two hands>: Holding up his hands, the speaker proves that external things exist.

<Two hands>

(1) Here is one hand, held up for the audience to see, and here is another, held up beside it.
-- Existential generalisation --
(2) Two human hands exist now.
(3) If two human hands exist now, then at least two things outside our minds exist now.
-- Modus ponens {uses: [2, 3]} --
(4) [External things exist]
